---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Site title="How the lab works"><div class="about"><span class="eyebrow">HOW THIS LAB WORKS</span><h1>From problem to explanation.</h1><p class="lede">The site is generated from the same exercise files you use locally. Your SQL remains runnable; the presentation adds context, evidence, and line-level reasoning.</p><div class="steps"><article><span>01</span><h2>Attempt</h2><p>Read the problem and run the synthetic schema and fixtures in the disposable PostGIS database. Write your own <code>attempt.sql</code>.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h2>Test</h2><p>Record edge cases and results in <code>tests.md</code>. Add a before or after CSV or image to show the change your SQL produced.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h2>Explain</h2><p>Use <code>annotations.yml</code> to attach the reason for important decisions to your SQL lines. Only then inspect the CanPermits implementation.</p></article></div><section class="format"><h2>One annotation, one decision</h2><p>Line notes live beside your SQL, so the SQL file remains executable. An anchor phrase protects against silently misplaced annotations when you edit the file.</p><pre>- lines: 12-16<br />  anchor: "a distinctive phrase on those lines"<br />  title: Boundary decision<br />  why: "Why I chose this behavior and what I tested."<br />  evidence: "See tests.md, shared-edge case."</pre><p>Hover gives a short preview. Click or keyboard focus selects the note in a persistent panel. Add <code>before.csv</code>, <code>after.csv</code>, or an image and reference it in <code>evidence.yml</code>.</p></section><a class="button" href={`${base}/#curriculum`}>Browse exercises →</a></div></Site>
<style>.about{max-width:1050px;margin:auto;padding:5rem 4vw}.about h1{max-width:800px}.lede{font-size:1.15rem;color:var(--muted);max-width:700px}.steps{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1.5rem;margin:4rem 0}.steps article{padding:1.5rem;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;background:white}.steps span{font:600 .78rem 'DM Mono',monospace;color:var(--teal)}.steps h2{font-size:1.8rem}.steps p,.format p{color:var(--muted)}.format{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:2rem 0 3rem}.format pre{background:#172933;color:#e9f3f0;border-radius:10px;padding:1.3rem;overflow-x:auto;font:13px/1.6 'DM Mono',monospace}.about code{font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:.85em}@media(max-width:720px){.steps{grid-template-columns:1fr}.about{padding:3rem 5vw}}</style>
